# DETAILS-NEG-CLIP: a vector field in Details (ImGuiUtilities::VectorField -- Location/Rotation/Scale and every reflected
# vec2/3/4) shows its number from the FIRST character, minus sign included, like UE's numeric entry: centred while it fits,
# otherwise cut on the right. Before: DragFloat started an overflowing value at the frame's left pixel, under the axis edge.
Дано run Entity Cube
Дано run View "View mode: Lit"
Когда --subject selection set Translation -253.2,-868.0,-12345.6
Тогда 1_neg_loc Details at its default width: Location starts "-253", "-868", "-123" - minus sign and first digits visible, the end cut on the right (the default value column is ~55 points a field)
# Widen Details: drag the viewport|Details dock splitter (window point x=1727) left to x=1500.
Когда input move - 1727,411
Когда input press - 1727,411
Когда input move - 1600,411
Когда input move - 1500,411
Когда input release - 1500,411
Тогда 1b_wide Details widened: Location reads "-253.2", "-868.0", "-12345.6" whole, each with its minus sign
# Narrow Details: the splitter from x=1500 to x=1800.
Когда input move - 1500,411
Когда input press - 1500,411
Когда input move - 1650,411
Когда input move - 1800,411
Когда input release - 1800,411
Тогда 2_narrow Details narrowed: each Location field shows its minus sign and first digits, the END of the number is cut
# Put the splitter back where the run found it: ImGui saves the dock sizes to Saved/Config/EditorLayout.ini, and the
# next run's drags start at x=1727.
Когда input move - 1800,411
Когда input press - 1800,411
Когда input move - 1760,411
Когда input move - 1727,411
